# ML data & evaluation discipline

## Data integrity

- Splits are ALWAYS chronological (oldest 70% / 15% / newest 15%). Never a random split.
- Label is `is_account_takeover` (ultra-rare: 141 positive rows total).
- `is_attack_ip` is leakage-sensitive: reserved for the A/B leakage comparison only,
  never the training target.
- Exclude non-human sentinel accounts (`--max-user-logins`, the ~14M-login id).
- Treat `"-"`/NaN as missing (RTT ~94% missing; region/city ~42% missing).

## Modelling

- Freeman likelihood-ratio model is the PRIMARY scorer (learns "normal", needs few
  labels). LogReg/RF/LightGBM/XGBoost are reference baselines only.

## Metrics (never headline plain accuracy)

- Report PR-AUC, recall @ a fixed low FPR (≤1%), and challenge rate.
- Always break metrics down BY history depth (40% of users have a single login and
  can't be protected by behavioural RBA yet).

## Dataset framing (for any write-up)

Wiefling RBA dataset is a privacy-preserving synthesis of real data — cite Wiefling
et al. (2022); rely on per-user consistency/imbalance/temporal signals; do NOT claim
real-world geolocation or IP-reputation performance.
